---
import {
  bastionImage,
  matthiasChurchImage,
  heroesSquareImage,
  basilicaImage,
  operaImage,
  bastionDayImage,
} from "../data/images"
---

<section
  id="monuments"
  class="relative bg-background-alt py-section palette-surface-light"
  aria-labelledby="monuments-heading"
  data-monuments
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-landing px-container-x sm:px-8 xl:px-14">
    <p
      class="reveal mb-6 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted"
    >
      Monumental Budapest
    </p>

    <h2
      id="monuments-heading"
      class="reveal max-w-heading font-display text-headline-1 font-bold leading-[1.05] text-foreground"
    >
      Stone, Light, Memory
    </h2>

    <p
      class="reveal mt-6 max-w-copy text-base leading-relaxed text-muted sm:text-lg"
    >
      Budapest's architecture is not a single style but a conversation between
      centuries — Romanesque foundations, Gothic spires, Baroque palaces,
      Neo-Renaissance facades, and Art Nouveau details layered one upon another.
    </p>

    <!-- Parliament — fullscreen image -->
    <figure class="reveal mt-16 sm:mt-20" data-monument-reveal="scale">
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
        <img
          src={`${bastionDayImage.src}&w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80`}
          srcset={`${bastionDayImage.src}&w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 800w, ${bastionDayImage.src}&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 1200w, ${bastionDayImage.src}&w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 1600w`}
          sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 90vw, 1200px"
          alt={bastionDayImage.alt}
          title={`Photo by ${bastionDayImage.author} on Unsplash`}
          width={bastionDayImage.width}
          height={bastionDayImage.height}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          class="photo-tone aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted">
        Photo by <a
          href={bastionDayImage.authorUrl}
          class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          rel="noopener">{bastionDayImage.author}</a
        >
        on <a
          href={bastionDayImage.unsplashUrl}
          class="underline hover:text-foreground"
          rel="noopener">Unsplash</a
        >
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <!-- Fisherman's Bastion + Matthias Church — two-column -->
    <div class="mt-20 grid gap-8 sm:mt-28 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-10">
      <!-- Fisherman's Bastion -->
      <div class="reveal" data-monument-reveal="mask">
        <figure>
          <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
            <img
              src={`${bastionImage.src}&w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80`}
              srcset={`${bastionImage.src}&w=400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 400w, ${bastionImage.src}&w=600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 600w, ${bastionImage.src}&w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 800w`}
              sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 45vw, 500px"
              alt={bastionImage.alt}
              title={`Photo by ${bastionImage.author} on Unsplash`}
              width={bastionImage.width}
              height={bastionImage.height}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              class="photo-tone aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted">
            Photo by <a
              href={bastionImage.authorUrl}
              class="underline hover:text-foreground"
              rel="noopener">{bastionImage.author}</a
            >
            on <a
              href={bastionImage.unsplashUrl}
              class="underline hover:text-foreground"
              rel="noopener">Unsplash</a
            >
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h3 class="mt-5 font-display text-headline-3 font-bold text-foreground">
          Fisherman's Bastion
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Built between 1895 and 1902 to the designs of Frigyes Schulek, the
          Bastion's seven turrets represent the seven Magyar tribes that settled
          in the Carpathian Basin in 895. A Neo-Romanesque terrace offering the
          city's most celebrated panorama of Parliament and the Danube.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Matthias Church -->
      <div class="reveal lg:mt-12" data-monument-reveal="rise">
        <figure>
          <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
            <img
              src={`${matthiasChurchImage.src}&w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80`}
              srcset={`${matthiasChurchImage.src}&w=400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 400w, ${matthiasChurchImage.src}&w=600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 600w, ${matthiasChurchImage.src}&w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 800w`}
              sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 45vw, 500px"
              alt={matthiasChurchImage.alt}
              title={`Photo by ${matthiasChurchImage.author} on Unsplash`}
              width={matthiasChurchImage.width}
              height={matthiasChurchImage.height}
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
              class="photo-tone aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted">
            Photo by <a
              href={matthiasChurchImage.authorUrl}
              class="underline hover:text-foreground"
              rel="noopener">{matthiasChurchImage.author}</a
            >
            on <a
              href={matthiasChurchImage.unsplashUrl}
              class="underline hover:text-foreground"
              rel="noopener">Unsplash</a
            >
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <h3 class="mt-5 font-display text-headline-3 font-bold text-foreground">
          Matthias Church
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Officially the Church of Our Lady, its foundations date to 1255. Named
          after King Matthias Corvinus who held both his weddings here in the
          15th century. The colorful Zsolnay ceramic tiles on its roof were
          added during Frigyes Schulek's 19th-century restoration.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Heroes' Square — wide + overlaid text -->
    <div class="reveal relative mt-20 sm:mt-28" data-monument-reveal="wide">
      <figure>
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
          <img
            src={`${heroesSquareImage.src}&w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80`}
            srcset={`${heroesSquareImage.src}&w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 800w, ${heroesSquareImage.src}&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 1200w, ${heroesSquareImage.src}&w=1600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 1600w`}
            sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 90vw, 1200px"
            alt={heroesSquareImage.alt}
            title={`Photo by ${heroesSquareImage.author} on Unsplash`}
            width={heroesSquareImage.width}
            height={heroesSquareImage.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="photo-tone aspect-[21/9] w-full object-cover"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted">
          Photo by <a
            href={heroesSquareImage.authorUrl}
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
            rel="noopener">{heroesSquareImage.author}</a
          >
          on <a
            href={heroesSquareImage.unsplashUrl}
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
            rel="noopener">Unsplash</a
          >
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="mt-5">
        <h3 class="font-display text-headline-2 font-bold text-foreground">
          Heroes' Square
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-2 max-w-lg text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Built for Hungary's Millennial celebrations in 1896, the square
          features the Millennium Monument — a 36-meter column topped by the
          Archangel Gabriel, flanked by colonnades bearing statues of Hungary's
          most important historical leaders. A UNESCO World Heritage Site since
          2002.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Basilica + Opera — two-column -->
    <div class="mt-20 grid gap-8 sm:mt-28 lg:grid-cols-5 lg:gap-12">
      <figure class="reveal lg:col-span-2" data-monument-reveal="vertical">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
          <img
            src={`${basilicaImage.src}&w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80`}
            srcset={`${basilicaImage.src}&w=400&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 400w, ${basilicaImage.src}&w=600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 600w, ${basilicaImage.src}&w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 800w`}
            sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 40vw, 400px"
            alt={basilicaImage.alt}
            title={`Photo by ${basilicaImage.author} on Unsplash`}
            width={basilicaImage.width}
            height={basilicaImage.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="photo-tone aspect-square w-full object-cover"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted">
          Photo by <a
            href={basilicaImage.authorUrl}
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
            rel="noopener">{basilicaImage.author}</a
          >
          on <a
            href={basilicaImage.unsplashUrl}
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
            rel="noopener">Unsplash</a
          >
        </figcaption>
        <h3 class="mt-5 font-display text-headline-3 font-bold text-foreground">
          St. Stephen's Basilica
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The largest church in Budapest, completed in 1905 after 54 years of
          construction. Its dome, at 96 meters, matches Parliament's height
          exactly — by law, no building in Budapest may exceed this.
        </p>
      </figure>

      <figure class="reveal lg:col-span-3" data-monument-reveal="clip">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-sm">
          <img
            src={`${operaImage.src}&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80`}
            srcset={`${operaImage.src}&w=600&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 600w, ${operaImage.src}&w=900&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 900w, ${operaImage.src}&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80 1200w`}
            sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 60vw, 700px"
            alt={operaImage.alt}
            title={`Photo by ${operaImage.author} on Unsplash`}
            width={operaImage.width}
            height={operaImage.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="photo-tone aspect-[4/3] w-full object-cover"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted">
          Photo by <a
            href={operaImage.authorUrl}
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
            rel="noopener">{operaImage.author}</a
          >
          on <a
            href={operaImage.unsplashUrl}
            class="underline hover:text-foreground"
            rel="noopener">Unsplash</a
          >
        </figcaption>
        <h3 class="mt-5 font-display text-headline-3 font-bold text-foreground">
          Hungarian State Opera
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-2 max-w-lg text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Designed by Miklos Ybl and opened in 1884, the Opera House on Andrassy
          Avenue is considered one of the most beautiful in Europe. Emperor
          Franz Joseph I attended the opening but stipulated that it must not
          outshine the Vienna Opera in size.
        </p>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
